        "original_id": "5ed7941b-60f0-509d-9939-55fdcb785d68",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Amer, William Shakespeare, Good\n- Works: The Tempest, Arrow in the Air, Catch My Soul, Othello\n- Places: Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire\n- Topics: acting, stage musicals, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote The Tempest around 1610–11, and many critics consider it the last play he wrote alone.\n- Nicholas Amer was born Thomas Harold Amer on 29 September 1923 in Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire.\n- Nicholas Amer is an English stage, film, and television actor known for performing in William Shakespeare’s plays.\n- Nicholas Amer made his professional debut in 1948 as Ferdinand in The Tempest.\n- Arrow in the Air starred Nicholas Amer.\n- Catch My Soul was an adaptation of Good’s stage musical of the same title, and that musical was loosely adapted from William Shakespeare’s Othello.",
